CAVEAT (2026-10-06): the Beatty gate 1 - {l log2 3} < (l+2)/(3 X ln 2) is linear in l, so sums and small multiples of
qualifying lengths qualify as well: the residual set is the Bohr set B(X) = {l : 1 - {l log2 3} < (l+2)/(3 X ln 2)},
of which this list shows only the convergents and intermediate fractions.  The SMALLEST residual length is still the
first upper convergent denominator past sqrt(3 X ln 2 / 2), because below that bound the gate forces a convergent.
The brute-force script (collatz_last_dip_residual_20261005.py) enumerates B(X) exactly for l <= 1e5.
